# Local chain deployment output. The directory itself is tracked (via
# .gitkeep) but its contents are not: docker-compose bind-mounts it, and Docker
# creates a missing bind-mount source as root:root — which the deliberately
# non-root chain-deploy service then cannot write into. Shipping the directory
# means a fresh clone already has it, owned by the user who cloned.
.deploy/*
!.deploy/.gitkeep
# The operator's own gateway configuration. `config-demo.yaml` is the one this
# repository ships and docker compose runs; `config.yaml` is whatever the
# person working here points at their own backend, and it is not ours to
# commit. `agent-commerce init` writes this name by default.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored `config.yaml` matches at every
# depth, which silently excluded all four examples/*/config.yaml from the
# repository. They existed locally, so the test that validates them passed —
# and failed the moment CI checked out a tree that had never contained them.
/config.yaml

.vite/
.turbo/
graphify-out/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.internal-docs

# npm package build output and local tarballs from `npm pack`.
*.tgz
